{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Ham, the father of Canaan.</b> Why was it necessary to say this here? Because the passage is engaged with and deals with Noah's drunkenness, in which Ham sinned and through which Canaan was cursed — and the genealogy of Ham has not yet been written, so we would not know that Canaan was his son. Therefore it was necessary to state here 'and Ham, the father of Canaan.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:08.300838070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}